# LIBRARY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM USING JAVA

## 1. Introduction

The Library Management System is a software application developed using Java to manage the daily activities of a library efficiently. It helps librarians maintain book records, student details, book issuing and returning information.

In a traditional library system, maintaining records manually takes more time and may lead to errors. This project provides a computerized solution that makes library operations easier, faster and more organized.

The application uses **Java Swing** for the graphical user interface and **SQLite** for storing data.

## 2. Problem Statement

Traditional library management involves maintaining books, student information and issue records manually. This process can result in data duplication, record loss, calculation errors and difficulty in tracking issued books.

Therefore, a computerized Library Management System is required to simplify library activities and maintain accurate records.

## 3. Objectives

- To develop an easy-to-use library management application.
- To maintain book details digitally.
- To store and manage student information.
- To simplify book issuing and returning.
- To track available and issued books.
- To reduce manual work and paperwork.
- To provide accurate and organized library records.

